    {
      "@id": "concept:c2014c00733-sch-4-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Schedule(s)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2014c00733#sch-4-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2014c00733.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2014c00733.pdf, p.6",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each Act, and each regulation, that is specified in a Schedule to\nthis Act is amended or repealed as set out in the applicable items in\nthe Schedule concerned, and any other item in a Schedule to this\nAct has effect according to its terms.\n\n(2) The amendment of any regulation under subsection (1) does not\nprevent the regulation, as so amended, from being amended or\nrepealed by the Governor-General.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, regulations amended under subsection (1) are\ntaken to still be regulations.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00733\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 4\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority (Consequential and\nTransitional Provisions) Act 2005",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each Act, and each regulation, that is specified in a Schedule to\nthis Act is amended or repealed as set out in the applicable items in\nthe Schedule concerned, and any other item in a Schedule to this\nAct has effect according to its terms.\n\n(2) The amendment of any regulation under subsection (1) does not\nprevent the regulation, as so amended, from being amended or\nrepealed by the Governor-General.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, regulations amended under subsection (1) are\ntaken to still be regulations.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2014C00733\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 4\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority (Consequential and\nTransitional Provisions) Act 2005",
